      say="Chunking splits source documents into smaller pieces before embedding and indexing, because you cannot embed a 100-page PDF as one vector and expect useful retrieval. Embedding models have input limits, one vector cannot represent fifty topics, and the LLM context window is finite. The chunk is the unit of retrieval. A good baseline is fixed-size chunks of 500 to 1,000 tokens with 10 to 20 percent overlap, or recursive splitting on paragraphs, then sentences, then words. Better options respect structure, split semantically, or index small chunks but return their larger parent.",
